long_description = "Ground cooked by old magma intrusions and still warm to the touch. Crystallized flows crack into sharp edges; the air tastes of sulfur, and the brightest veins will char anything that lingers. Useful minerals sit just below the crust where the heat hasn't gotten to them yet."
